aarch64 getcontext/setcontext/makecontext/swapcontext -- NOT BUILT, NOT VERIFIED

This directory is deliberately not named "aarch64", so the Makefile ignores
it and Kinetic on aarch64 behaves as musl does (the functions are declared
but not defined).

State: the code assembles and links for aarch64, and the ucontext_t offsets
it hardcodes are checked at compile time. The aarch64 test binary built
against it segfaulted immediately under qemu-user 8.2.2 (before main printed
anything), and the cause was not isolated: it could be this code, the
cross-toolchain, or qemu. Do not enable it until
`tests/compat.c` passes on real hardware or a known-good emulator.

To try it: rename this directory to "aarch64", build with a cross compiler,
and run tests/run.sh with KINETIC_AARCH64_CROSS and KINETIC_QEMU_AARCH64 set.
